==English==
{{was wotd|2024|August|5}}

===Etymology===
{{PIE word|en|upó}}{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₁lewdʰ-}}
[[File:Harpocrate dieu du silence - det.jpg|thumb|{{w|Louis-Philippe Mouchy}}, ''Harpocrate, dieu du silence'' (''Harpocrates, the God of Silence'', 1789). In [[Ancient Greek#Adjective|Ancient Greek]] [[mythology]], {{w|Harpocrates}} was given a [[rose#Noun|rose]] by {{w|Eros}} to [[ensure]] that the [[sexual#Adjective|sexual]] [[indiscretion]]s of Eros’s mother {{w|Aphrodite}} were not revealed. This is said to have led the rose to become a [[symbol#Noun|symbol]] of [[secrecy]].]]

The {{glossary|adverb}} and {{glossary|adjective}} are an {{ubor|en|LL.|sub rosā|lit=under the rose|nocap=1}}, from {{der|en|la|sub|t=beneath, under}} + {{m|la|rosa|t=rose}} (possibly from {{der|en|grc|ῥόδον|t=rose}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ira-pro|*wardah|t=flower; rose}} and {{der|en|ine-pro|*Hwerdʰ-}}, possibly a {{glossary|metathesis}} of {{m|ine-pro|*h₁lewdʰ-|t=to grow; to rise}}). The reason for the reference to a rose is uncertain,<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=adv.'' and ''adj|id=4635478096|date=July 2023|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=adj.'' and ''adv|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220722100940/https://www.lexico.com/definition/sub_rosa}}</ref> though it has been suggested that it derives from the Ancient Greek myth that {{w|Aphrodite}} (the goddess of love) gave a rose to her son {{w|Eros}} (the god of love and sex), who in turn gave it to {{w|Harpocrates}} (the god of silence, confidentiality, and secrets) to ensure that Aphrodite’s sexual indiscretions were not revealed.<ref>{{R:Dictionary.com|pos=adv}}</ref> Roses thus became a symbol of secrecy—they were, for example, used at meetings to pledge the participants not to disclose what had been discussed. Compare {{m|en|under the rose}} which is attested earlier.<ref>{{R:OED Online|subentry=under the rose|subpos=phrase|entry=rose|pos=''n.''{{sup|1}} and ''adj.''{{sup|1}}|noformat=1|id=5317809334|date=July 2024}}</ref><ref>{{R:Collins English Dictionary|entry=under the rose}}</ref>

The {{glossary|noun}} is derived from the adverb and adjective.

